== one document, and something typed into it ==
  open:  true
  tabs:  ["main.bas"]
  typed: [typed by hand, never saved]
== a second document opens: the tab set GROWS ==
  reconciled: 2
  tabs:  ["main.bas","README.md"]
  KEPT:  [typed by hand, never saved]
== the first is edited: the CAPTION moves, the editor does not ==
  tabs:  ["* main.bas","README.md"]
  KEPT:  [typed by hand, never saved]
  (the marker is in the caption, where the GTK notebook puts it --
   a reconcile re-reads it, and the tab is keyed on the document id)
== and the first closes: the tab set SHRINKS ==
  tabs:  ["README.md"]
== and reopening it mints a NEW document, so a new editor ==
   (that a dropped widget is DELETED rather than hidden is gBASIC's
    own claim, held there by a source tripwire -- a widget nobody can
    name is unobservable from this side, which is why it has to be)
  tabs:  ["README.md","main.bas"]
  ed_doc_3: []
